{"title":"Quadratic residues","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a>, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/c/b0c7d9710367d9bb32d3fd8488f4e13c6eefc84c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" />. We say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a <b>quadratic residue</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Modulo\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Modulo\">modulo</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> if there is some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/561468d227c8facbe502dc46a5087c5e4d4a61b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2-a$\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Divisibility\" title=\"Divisibility\"> divisible</a> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Legendre_Symbol\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Legendre Symbol</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Quadratic_Reciprocity\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Quadratic Reciprocity</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Additional_properties\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Additional properties</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Jacobi_Symbol\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Jacobi Symbol</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Calculation_and_examples\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Calculation and examples</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#The_general_case\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The general case</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Legendre_Symbol\">Legendre Symbol</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_residues&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Legendre Symbol\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determining whether <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a quadratic residue modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is easiest if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a07ccbb6f446bd3ddd9b870c17f10cf188e5399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"11\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime_number\" title=\"Prime number\">prime</a>. In this case we write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc444845b2cf7bb96e493949c4a85aca6c46ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{a}{p}\\right)=\\begin{cases} 0 &amp; \\mathrm{if }\\ p\\mid a, \\\\ 1 &amp; \\mathrm{if }\\ p\\nmid a\\ \\mathrm{ and }\\ a\\ \\mathrm{\\ is\\ a\\ quadratic\\ residue\\ modulo\\ }\\ p, \\\\ -1 &amp; \\mathrm{if }\\ p\\nmid a\\ \\mathrm{ and }\\ a\\ \\mathrm{\\ is\\ a\\ quadratic\\ nonresidue\\ modulo\\ }\\ p. \\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -33px\" width=\"518\" height=\"75\" /> \n</p><p>The symbol <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/4/9d4dbd6ad996cd00a817ea92c848b273c324c8b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{a}{p}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"36\" height=\"43\" /> is called the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre_symbol&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Legendre symbol (page does not exist)\">Legendre symbol</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Quadratic_Reciprocity\">Quadratic Reciprocity</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_residues&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Quadratic Reciprocity\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be distinct <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Odd_integer\" title=\"Odd integer\"> odd</a> primes. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/1/c61a3e22866c892043f24f75a3f331824d93cde4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{p}{q}\\right)\\left(\\frac{q}{p}\\right)=(-1)^{\\frac{p-1}{2}\\frac{q-1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"190\" height=\"43\" />. This is known as the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_Reciprocity_Theorem\" title=\"Quadratic Reciprocity Theorem\">Quadratic Reciprocity Theorem</a>.\nWhereas the above are properties of the Legendre symbol, they still hold for any odd coprime integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> when using the Jacobi symbol defined below.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Additional_properties\">Additional properties</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_residues&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Additional properties\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Also, we have for any odd prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> the following rules:\n</p><p>Multiplicativity: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/152bd191e3c52cc7dd79283e57e06124aa7c619a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{a}{p}\\right) \\left(\\frac{b}{p}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{ab}{p}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"150\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Euler's criterion: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b471167edc83d42da5a9197e31ba7e633bae7e84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{a}{p}\\right) \\equiv a^{\\frac{p-1}{2}} \\mod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"161\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>First supplementary rule: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/c/5bc9e888dec1f232a5adf6b5211b40e11331eb83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{-1}{p}\\right)=(-1)^{\\frac{p-1}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"138\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/a/66a1114a3212adac4f386e875ae32dc0a5a767b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{-1}{p}\\right)=1 \\iff p \\equiv 1 \\mod 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"244\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Second supplementary rule: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08f6a07d478b6d7d63e417ad466f84aa66a7ea30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{2}{p}\\right)=(-1)^{\\frac{p^2-1}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"130\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c6299759fcdec5f6a9ea0a413a4a76c3989dff73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{2}{p}\\right)=1 \\iff p \\equiv \\pm 1 \\mod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"244\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>It's also useful not to forget that the symbols are only properties <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f965eb9407014fe0e4fc671eed0acbfd84eddb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/9/389fbab887350454d648dc440ffe44e890ac4ed7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\equiv b \\mod p \\implies \\left(\\frac{a}{p}\\right)=\\left(\\frac{b}{p}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"253\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Jacobi_Symbol\">Jacobi Symbol</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_residues&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Jacobi Symbol\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Now suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/b/09b93d65d5c894ba13dcf207808e94ecdd5eada1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=p_1^{e_1}\\cdots p_n^{e_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"17\" />. Then we write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f23bbc8040fd433e639a73237dd4794dafc2f38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{a}{m}\\right)=\\left(\\frac{a}{p_1}\\right)^{e_1}\\cdots\\left(\\frac{a}{p_n}\\right)^{e_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"215\" height=\"44\" />. This symbol is called the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Jacobi_symbol&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Jacobi symbol (page does not exist)\">Jacobi symbol</a>.\nAll properties mentioned above except Euler's criterion are also true for Jacobi symbols with odd (positive) integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> instead.\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f82055228dcb80c7f12c8c16d14008c8a18ee43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{a}{m}\\right)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"73\" height=\"33\" /> does not mean that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a quadratic residue <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/a/88a41e81d2aba832835545f45e0c8f8aa7f5e9aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod m$\" width=\"68\" height=\"12\" /> (but is necessary for it to be).\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Calculation_and_examples\">Calculation and examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_residues&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Calculation and examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>With the rules and properties already mentioned, it's eays to calculate Jacobi symbols. Since they are for primes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> identical to the Legendre symbol, this gives a fast way to decide if an integer is a quadratic residue <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f965eb9407014fe0e4fc671eed0acbfd84eddb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mod p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> or not.\n</p><p>Example:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/a/d9adf0f8993ba0bcca0ddd1d899dad61ef2858e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{12345}{13337}\\right) =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"94\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/e/b9e4cc4bf330ff13ee52d74e921c0e485172b3b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\left(\\frac{13337}{12345}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{992}{12345}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{2^5}{12345}\\right)\\left(\\frac{31}{12345}\\right)=\\left(\\frac{2}{12345}\\right)^5 \\left(\\frac{12345}{31}\\right)=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"577\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e90ee1087600650954190a3d08b85c88f8862df5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 1^5 \\left(\\frac{7}{31}\\right) = -\\left(\\frac{31}{7}\\right) = -\\left(\\frac{3}{7}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{7}{3}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"403\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/4/0640818a6197f2736b3259f8a356f0fb27556268.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Thus we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/7/70721c830aa84eadb8417a0352d5ae02ead8d5bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12345$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> is a quadratic residue <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Modulo\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Modulo\">modulo</a> the prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6c469c7ae1b2f9973f3fedcd23170ef1cadfac1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13337$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />. Indeed: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30cdc212f83ea50bc2263669f5aa84a18e4590db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2425^2 \\equiv 12345 \\mod 13337$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"211\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>In a more general manner, one, for example, also gets:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/c/bdc1aab3d038991d3a932ae049ee9acde4f2782d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{-2}{p}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{-1}{p}\\right)\\left(\\frac{2}{p}\\right) = (-1)^{\\frac{(p-2)^2-1}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"288\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/e/b9e7bbe926b288a27241f349c7bd8f4efcf4a735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{-2}{p}\\right)=1 \\iff p \\equiv 1,3 \\mod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"261\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/9/dc935ffda2e406793663f3be753ca2c826ff6355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{3}{p}\\right) = (-1)^{\\frac{p-1}{2}} \\left(\\frac{p}{3}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"161\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1dde16bbc0e774af99efdfbfb62fdc80bd4d9f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{3}{p}\\right)=1 \\iff p \\equiv \\pm 1 \\mod 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"256\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/289d2b3dfc64ef4ee0ae9dca4ae7fa1a9dc35cdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{-3}{p}\\right) = \\left(\\frac{p}{3}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"109\" height=\"43\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/f/61f1ea62806995f3058a5ad9a83764b3f52eb2f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{-3}{p}\\right)=1 \\iff p \\equiv 1 \\mod 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"244\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_general_case\">The general case</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_residues&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: The general case\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In general, to determine whether <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a quadratic residue modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, one has to check whether <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a quadratic residue modulo every odd prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. This is enough if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f28f7175430049f8e55d0a8fd07d6b710bf2b03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2m$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is odd. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/2/4223cdf3271444d6449bf91b3e23fd86ea06b442.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=4m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is odd, one also has to check that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/072af1e298d0cc00268a303b6e415286744a6353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\equiv 0\\mathrm{\\ or\\ }1\\mod 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"141\" height=\"13\" />. Finally, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, one also has to check that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/b/eeb1b45a8776306d9de1620f20cde57a098502c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\equiv 0,1,\\mathrm{\\ or\\ }4\\mod 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"166\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018075340\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.034 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 319/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 12716/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2093:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018075340 and revision id 88717. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}